                <pb facs="0553" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <head>293. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in the United Kingdom<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d293-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-08-23T16:59:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1958—4:59 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2077. Gist Amman’s 596 and 597 to Department<anchor n="2" xml:id="d293-f2"/>
                    (repeated separately London) conveyed British Minister Lord Hood who undertook
                    to take matter up urgently with FornOff. Without going into Rifai’s
                    interpretation US/UK policies we told Hood it appeared to us Hussein and Rifai saw
                    handwriting on wall. In putting price for their continuing in business so high,
                    probably in realization we would be unable meet it, King and Rifai may be
                    seeking justify decision to get out. It was our view that precipitate departure
                    of King would be most undesirable although change of government might not be too
                    bad a development in post-GA atmosphere.</p>
                <p>US–HKJ treaty and massive financial and military
                    support out of question. Since it unlikely US could make public statement which
                    would satisfy King and Rifai, problem seemed to come down to whether limited
                    program of assurances and tangible support could be devised which would have
                    effect inducing King at least refrain from precipitate decision throw in his
                    cards.</p>
                <p>In view Jordanian request for reply prior SYG’s
                    departure from Jordan we hope have FornOff views early next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
